// GHZ state: three-qubit entanglement.
//
// Concept
//   The Bell construction extended: one Hadamard and two controlled-NOTs tie
//   three qubits into a single state where all three measurement outcomes
//   always agree.
//
// Expected quantum behaviour
//   (|000> + |111>)/sqrt(2).
//
// Expected measurement results
//   Only 000 and 111, roughly 50% each. Measuring any one qubit instantly
//   determines the other two.
//
// Mathematical interpretation
//   GHZ entanglement is qualitatively different from the three-party W state:
//   tracing out any one GHZ qubit leaves the other two *unentangled*, whereas
//   for W it does not. Both have all three qubits individually maximally mixed,
//   so single-qubit measurements alone cannot tell them apart.
//
// @expect qubits=3 clbits=3 gates=3
// @expect-state |000>=0.5
// @expect-state |111>=0.5
// @expect-support 000,111
// @expect-frequency 000=0.5

qubit[3] q;
bit[3] c;

h q[0];
cx q[0], q[1];
cx q[0], q[2];

measure q[0] -> c[0];
measure q[1] -> c[1];
measure q[2] -> c[2];
